        "source":  "CIO.com",
        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4222319/connecting-ai-agents-was-only-the-beginning-now-they-need-to-think-together.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-16",
        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "Cisco\u0027s Outshift group identifies a new frontier problem it calls the \u0027Internet of Cognition\u0027: AI agents can communicate across organizational boundaries but frequently fail at joint planning and collective reasoning. Research shows that simply passing messages between agents does not produce shared intent or coordinated action. Cisco and ServiceNow are collaborating on open-source projects like Mycelium to address shared context and human-understandable reasoning between multi-agent systems.",
        "execSummary":  "Connecting agents is a solved problem; getting them to reason together is not. Cisco\u0027s Internet of Cognition framing surfaces the next critical gap for enterprise AI programs: multi-agent systems that can pass messages but cannot align on intent will generate inconsistent, untrustworthy outcomes at scale. For customer-support leaders deploying agent chains across triage, fulfillment, and escalation, this is the architectural risk to test now before production scale. The practical action is auditing where hand-offs between agents assume shared context that was never explicitly established.",
