        "date":  "2026-09-16",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Roche CDTO Wafaa Mamilli describes the company\u0027s AI strategy as rooted in trusted data, governance, and measurable business outcomes rather than chasing technical certainty. Roche deploys AI across kidney disease prediction, digital pathology, drug discovery, and employee coaching. Mamilli credits organizational restructuring — including dedicated AI and data leadership roles — as essential to moving from pilots to enterprise-scale impact.",
        "execSummary":  "Roche\u0027s AI journey offers a validated blueprint for large enterprises: invest in data quality and governance first, build dedicated AI leadership, then deploy across high-value workflows. The emphasis on organizational structure over technology selection is the key insight — Mamilli\u0027s advice to pair business acumen with deep technical understanding applies directly to any enterprise standing up AI-led support or operations. The lesson for customer-support leaders is that AI ROI follows organizational readiness, not tool selection. Standing up an AI center of excellence or dedicated AI ownership before scaling agent deployments is the differentiating move.",
