        "date":  "2026-04-21",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "As AI agents proliferate across enterprises, the absence of proper controls is creating new security vulnerabilities. Deloitte research finds that while 74% of companies plan to deploy agentic AI within two years, only 21% have mature governance models in place. A centralized control plane — managing agent permissions, tracking actions, and preventing unsafe deployments at scale — is identified as the essential architectural requirement.",
